alta: program priority by process name, with a ring guard for lower priorities

hw_job_prio (0644) holds up to 16 rules "name=high|normal|low" (process name
as in /proc/<pid>/comm). A program gets its priority when it opens the NPU;
writing the table also moves programs that already have it open
(drm_sched_entity_set_priority + drm_sched_entity_modify_sched under
gpu->sched_lock, so drm_sched moves the entity to the new run queue at its
next quiet moment). Unnamed programs stay at normal, as in stock etnaviv.
Bad rules are skipped with a warning.

hw_job_clients (0444) lists the programs with the NPU open:
"<pid> <name> <priority> <applied|pending>".

hw_job_prio_guard_ms (0644, default 100, 0 = off): while a higher-priority
job has run within that time, a lower-priority job enters only an empty
ring, so a higher-priority job waits for at most one lower-priority job.

Applies on top of 0001-0006; touches etnaviv_drv.c, etnaviv_gpu.h and
etnaviv_sched.c.

